"Investment Spending Shock Analysis for Georgia",
"Macro Accounting Framework (Demand Side)",
,
"PROJECT OVERVIEW:",
"Investment Amount: USD 6.5 billion",
"Investment Period: 8 years (2026-2033)",
"Exchange Rate: 2.746 GEL/USD",
"Analysis Type: Demand-side impact on GDP",
,
"STEP-BY-STEP INSTRUCTIONS:",
,
"STEP 1: Data Collection from IMF WEO Database",
"1. Go to sheet ""WEO_Data""",
"2. Visit: https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/WEO/weo-database/2024/October",
"3. Select Country: Georgia",
"4. Select Indicators: Real GDP Growth (%), Nominal GDP (USD bn), GDP Deflator (Index)",
"5. Download data for years 2020-2029",
"6. Populate columns B, C, D in WEO_Data sheet (rows 4-13)",
"7. Formulas will automatically:",
"   - Extend 2027 real GDP growth rate to 2043",
"   - Extend GDP deflator using average 2020-2023 growth rate",
"   - Calculate Nominal GDP in GEL using exchange rate 2.746",
,
"STEP 2: Data Collection from geostat.ge (Supply and Use Tables)",
"1. Visit: https://www.geostat.ge/en/modules/categories/191/supply-use-tables",
"2. Download the latest Supply and Use Tables (Excel format)",
"3. Copy the SUPPLY table (38x38) to sheet ""SUPPLY""",
"4. Copy the USE table (38x38) to sheet ""USE""",
"5. Sheet ""SUT Calc"" will automatically:",
"   - Link data from SUPPLY and USE sheets",
"   - Calculate import content share (cell C46)",
"   - This value feeds into the NA sheet scenarios",
,
"STEP 3: Review Scenario Analysis",
"1. Go to sheet ""NA"" (National Accounts)",
"2. Review three scenarios:",
"   - Scenario 1 (Base Case): Demand multiplier = 0.8, Import share from SUT Calc",
"   - Scenario 2: Demand multiplier = 1.0 (higher multiplier effect)",
"   - Scenario 3: Import content share = 0.5 (higher import content)",
"3. All scenarios use bell-shaped project allocation over 8 years",
"4. Results show GDP impact, multiplier effects, and projected growth rates",
,
"SHEET GUIDE:",
"Instructions - This sheet (overview and guide)",
"WEO_Data - IMF World Economic Outlook data for Georgia",
"SUPPLY - Supply table from geostat (38x38)",
"USE - Use table from geostat (38x38)",
"SUT Calc - Calculations from Supply and Use tables",
"NA - National Accounts analysis with 3 scenarios",
,
"COLOR CODING:",
"Blue text","Hardcoded inputs (values you enter or assumptions)"
"Black text","Formulas and calculations"
"Green text","Links to other sheets within this workbook"
"Red text","Important notes or external data sources"
